    /* ---- Life Guard case ---- */
    "lg.title": "Life Guard",
    "lg.kicker": "Case 01 · 2021",
    "lg.sub":    "Prototype of an app for Life Tecnologia, where the client watches the security cameras installed in their home from their phone.",
    "lg.f1": "Client", "lg.v1": "Life Tecnologia",
    "lg.f2": "Role",   "lg.v2": "UI &amp; UX Design, prototyping",
    "lg.f3": "Scope",  "lg.v3": "iOS + Android app, 14 screens",
    "lg.f4": "Year",
    "lg.h1": "The context",
    "lg.c1": "<p>Life Tecnologia's own app for clients who subscribe to internet and security cameras. The manufacturer's stock software shipped with email and password login, English menus and no trace of the brand, which turned into recurring support calls with the same complaint: <i>I can't see my camera</i>.</p><p>The goal was an app where the client signs in with the number already on file and sees their house on the first screen.</p>",
    "lg.h2": "The process",
    "lg.c2": "<p>The flow is built around the shortest path between opening the app and seeing the camera. Sign-in is by phone number and validation code, with no password, followed by the profile screen, since the subscription belongs to the household and not to one person.</p><p>The home screen lists cameras by room name instead of channel number. The player opens live and reaches recordings by date in one tap, and the account menu gathers what used to be a phone call: users, plan, problem reports and support contact.</p><p>Exception states were part of the scope: unregistered number, empty search results and subscribers still in the installation queue. The interface is dark so video is the brightest element on screen, with brand orange reserved for action.</p>",
    "lg.h3": "The outcome",
    "lg.c3": "<p>A clickable prototype of 14 screens, from splash to editing a user, with error paths and empty states already resolved.</p><ul><li>Passwordless entry: phone number and validation code</li><li>Multiple profiles per subscription, without multiplying accounts</li><li>Error, empty-search and pre-installation states designed</li><li>Components and spacing built to translate straight into React Native</li></ul><p>The project stopped at the prototype, used by Life to discuss scope, effort and brand presence over a concrete version of the product.</p>",
    "lg.heroAlt": "Life Guard screens over the brand orange",
    "lg.ga": "Entry: from splash to profile",
    "lg.gb": "Daily use: cameras, player and account",
    "lg.gc": "States and management: what usually gets left out",
    "lg.g1":  "Splash",
    "lg.g2":  "Wi-Fi notice",
    "lg.g3":  "Sign in by phone",
    "lg.g4":  "Validation code",
    "lg.g5":  "Who's watching",
